hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2743","Narrated to us 'Abdul-Jabbar ibnul-'Ala', who said:\nNarrated to us Sufyan, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Nafi', who said:\nIbn 'Umar intended to perform Hajj, so he said: \"Make it an 'Umrah. If I am prevented, then I will do as the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did.\"\nWhen he approached al-Bayda', he said: \"I do not see the path between them except as one. And I call you to witness that I have made Hajj obligatory along with my 'Umrah.\"\nWhen he reached Qudayd, he bought a sacrificial animal and drove it with him until he arrived in Makkah. He performed Tawaf around the House, prayed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam, and performed Sa'i between Safa and Marwah. He said: \"This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) do.\"\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
"2744","Narrated to us al-‘Abbās ibn ‘Abd al-‘Azīm and Yaḥyā ibn Ḥakīm, both said: Narrated to us ‘Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī, who said: Narrated to us Mālik ibn Anas, on the authority of al-Zuhrī, from ‘Urwah, from ‘Ā’ishah (RA), that the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) who performed *Qirān* (combined Hajj and ‘Umrah) made one *Ṭawāf* (circumambulation).\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
"2745","###\n Narrated to us by Hisham bin Yunus bin Wail bin Waddah, who said: Narrated to us by Ibn al-Darawardi, on the authority of Ubaydullah, on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of Ibn Umar (RA), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \"Whoever enters the state of Ihram for both Hajj and 'Umrah (Qiran), one Tawaf will suffice for both of them; then he should not exit the state of"
"2746","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, narrated to us 'Amr ibn 'Uthman al-Kilabi, narrated to us Dawud ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-'Attar, on the authority of Musa ibn 'Uqbah, on the authority of Nafi', on the authority of Ibn 'Umar (RA) that he combined Hajj and 'Umrah (Qiran) and performed a single Tawaf for both. He said, \"This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) do it.\"\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
